"""Reference-velocity source location and migration-design research code.

This preserved-source revision adds a leakage-free robust closed loop: 
spatially correlated velocity perturbations are propagated by FMM into full path-related travel-time covariance; 
known calibration-source residuals form an empirical bias field; 
receivers and calibration sources are selected jointly using mean error, CVaR tail error, interval coverage, and sharpness.  
Training, interval-calibration, design-validation, and untouched out-of-distribution test velocity splits are independent.  
Six requested baselines, paired block bootstrap, and station-failure audits are written by the main workflow.

This extended preserved-source revision also adds a fixed localization +
travel-time-posterior migration case.  It evaluates every held-out model/event
block, includes a full-versus-diagonal path-covariance ablation, and writes nine
comparison figures whose titles name the data-driven winner rather than assuming
that the proposed method wins every metric.
"""

